WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.418
Hi! One, two, three... let's count to 10. Today we'll learn numbers up to 10: counting, reading, writing and comparing.

2
00:00:11.568 --> 00:00:17.322
When counting, touch each thing once. Don't skip any and don't count any twice.

3
00:00:17.472 --> 00:00:20.946
The last number you say tells how many there are.

4
00:00:21.096 --> 00:00:23.826
When there is nothing, that's 0.

5
00:00:23.976 --> 00:00:29.730
Numbers can be written as numerals or words: 5 is five.

6
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.770
Line two rows up one to one. The row with extras has more.

7
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:40.362
Numbers that come later when counting are greater: 7 is greater than 5.

8
00:00:40.512 --> 00:00:45.162
One more than 6 is 7, and one less than 6 is 5.

9
00:00:45.312 --> 00:00:50.394
Smallest to greatest: 2, 5, 8.

10
00:00:50.544 --> 00:00:57.186
Watch out! 3 big watermelons and 5 small grapes: the watermelons are not more!

11
00:00:57.336 --> 00:01:01.698
To compare how many, count them. Size doesn't matter.

12
00:01:01.848 --> 00:01:06.834
5 is greater than 3, so there are more grapes.

13
00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:15.834
Your turn! Count the stars. How many are there? Pause and think.

14
00:01:15.984 --> 00:01:21.666
Counting one by one, there are 6. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:21.816 --> 00:01:30.426
Another one! Which is greater, 8 or 6? Pause and think.

16
00:01:30.576 --> 00:01:36.546
8 comes after 6, so 8 is greater. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:44.778
Here's another! What is one more than 4? Pause and think.

18
00:01:44.928 --> 00:01:50.250
The number after 4 is 5. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:58.578
Try one more! What is one less than 9? Pause and think.

20
00:01:58.728 --> 00:02:04.242
The number before 9 is 8. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:04.392 --> 00:02:12.330
Try one more! Which numeral is seven? Pause and think.

22
00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.250
Seven is 7. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:27.642
Try one more! Put 9, 3 and 6 in order from smallest to greatest. Pause and think.

24
00:02:27.792 --> 00:02:34.122
The smallest is 3, then 6, then 9. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:34.272 --> 00:02:42.618
Last one! Which is smaller, 10 or 4? Pause and think.

26
00:02:42.768 --> 00:02:48.978
4 comes before 10, so 4 is smaller. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:49.128 --> 00:02:55.914
Remember: count one by one, and the last number is how many. Numbers that come later are greater.

28
00:02:56.064 --> 00:02:59.585
Count the chairs at home!

